% BEGIN of inlined logic: the rules of the decision checks, below, copy the
% decision service PersonNotEnrolledInBenefitService of the imported model
% PersonNotEnrolledInBenefit (person-not-enrolled-in-benefit.dmn); the
% decision service PersonEnrolledInBenefitService of the imported model
% PersonEnrolledInBenefit (person-enrolled-in-benefit.dmn).
% The copy keeps this program in one file. You may want to move the copied
% logic to a separate file of its own, and include that file in this program
% and in the other programs that use it ("the knowledge base ... includes
% these resources").
rule checks_1 with provenance the model at decision checks:
the not already on senior citizen tax freeze of the checks is true if
    the enrollments of the situation are listed
    and the primary person id of the situation is a text
    and it is not the case that
        the enrollments of the situation include a person id with a benefit
        and the primary person id of the situation is the text
        and the person id is equal to the text
        and the benefit is equal to "PhlSeniorCitizenTaxFreeze".

rule checks_2 with provenance the model at decision checks:
the not already on senior citizen tax freeze of the checks is false if
    the enrollments of the situation are listed
    and the enrollments of the situation include a person id with a benefit
    and the person id is equal to the primary person id of the situation
    and the benefit is equal to "PhlSeniorCitizenTaxFreeze".

the owner occupant of the checks is the owner occupant service result, as stated in the model at decision checks.

the lives in philadelphia pa of the checks is the lives in philadelphia pa service result, as stated in the model at decision checks.

the meets age requirement of the checks is the sctf age requirement service result, as stated in the model at decision checks.

% END of inlined logic (decision checks).
rule is_eligible_1 with provenance the model at decision isEligible:
the is_eligible is true if
    the not already on senior citizen tax freeze of the checks is true
    and the owner occupant of the checks is true
    and the lives in philadelphia pa of the checks is true
    and the meets age requirement of the checks is true.

rule is_eligible_2 with provenance the model at decision isEligible:
the is_eligible is false if
    the not already on senior citizen tax freeze of the checks is false.

rule is_eligible_3 with provenance the model at decision isEligible:
the is_eligible is false if
    the owner occupant of the checks is false.

rule is_eligible_4 with provenance the model at decision isEligible:
the is_eligible is false if
    the lives in philadelphia pa of the checks is false.

rule is_eligible_5 with provenance the model at decision isEligible:
the is_eligible is false if
    the meets age requirement of the checks is false.

the apply url of the eligible of the next steps is "https://tax-services.phila.gov/_/".

the help url of the eligible of the next steps is "https://www.phila.gov/services/payments-assistance-taxes/payment-plans-and-assistance-programs/income-based-programs-for-residents/apply-for-the-low-income-senior-citizen-real-estate-tax-freeze/".

the help phone of the eligible of the next steps is "(215) 686-6442".

the body of the eligible of the next steps is "Apply through the Philadelphia Tax Center or use the paper application on the program page. You do not need an online account.

- Apply by September 30 each year. If you missed the deadline and are already 65 or older, ask Revenue about backdated enrollment.
- Include copies of proof of age and income for yourself and your spouse, as applicable. Keep your original documents.
- If you qualified in an earlier year, ask Revenue which year's income documents to provide.".

the note of the ineligible of the next steps is "Eligible residents of cooperative buildings use a special co-op application. Check the program page or contact Revenue for help with your situation.".

